Subject: Kernel Record Core V1
Date: 2026-05-26
Schema UUID: 2c9dc156-4d5d-49bc-a500-ebe06db00c10

@ [slice_authority] docs/slices/FSC1_Final_Slices.v1.sop
@ [canonical_slice_authority] docs/canonical/LangSOP_FSC1_Final_Slices.canonical.sop
@ [final_slicing_authority] docs/canonical/LangSOP_Final_Slicing_Surface.canonical.sop
@ [v2_canonical_authority] docs/canonical/LangSOP_Initial_Workflow.v2.canonical.sop

& [SchemaRecord: KernelRecordCoreV1] is the accepted common logical schema for LangSOP authority-kernel records
  + [schema_id] is kernel-record-core-v1
  + [schema_uuid] is 2c9dc156-4d5d-49bc-a500-ebe06db00c10
  + [slice_id] is FSC1-S01
  + [authority_scope] is common KernelRecord fields, shared enumerations, lineage invariants, freshness invariants, and acceptance checklist
  + [implementation_scope] is logical schema only
  + [next_dependent_slice] is FSC1-S02 record-specific schema and natural-key matrix

  = must: define the common field contract before record-specific schemas are finalized
  = must: distinguish source records, derived projections, accepted authority, proof-backed records, stale records, contradicted records, and invalidated records
  = must: preserve source_ref_set for every claim-bearing or derived record
  = must: preserve lineage_edge_set for every derived, projected, superseded, contradicted, invalidated, reviewed, or proof-backed record
  = must: preserve stale, contradicted, and invalidated records as trace
  = must: route unresolved identity, authority conflict, or freshness uncertainty to a blocked or fault-bearing record rather than hiding it
  - never: choose physical storage in this schema
  - never: define record-specific payload fields in this schema
  - never: implement LangGraph nodes, UI surfaces, dispatch, or operations control from this schema alone

| [KernelRecordKind] is (
  source_log |
  log_entry |
  citation_ref |
  narrative_node |
  understanding_anchor |
  capability_node |
  requirement_record |
  support_record |
  support_gap |
  authority_artifact |
  coordination_claim |
  operator_contract |
  operator_trace |
  work_packet |
  completion_review |
  readiness_projection |
  stale_projection |
  proof_result |
  fault_record
)

| [AuthorityState] is (
  none |
  source_only |
  narrative_projection |
  accepted_decision |
  signed_sjs |
  proof_backed |
  stale_projection |
  contradicted |
  invalidated |
  human_override
)

| [ReadinessState] is (
  not_applicable |
  desired |
  source_preserved |
  specified |
  supported |
  blocked |
  deferred |
  ready_to_packetize |
  packetized |
  assigned |
  implemented |
  verified |
  stale |
  superseded |
  contradicted
)

| [RecordStatus] is (
  draft |
  active |
  accepted |
  gated |
  blocked |
  completed |
  verified |
  stale |
  superseded |
  contradicted |
  invalidated
)

| [NaturalKeyState] is (
  accepted |
  candidate |
  composite |
  not_applicable |
  unresolved |
  superseded
)

| [FreshnessState] is (
  current |
  stale |
  unknown |
  not_applicable |
  invalidated
)

| [LineageEdgeKind] is (
  source_of |
  derived_from |
  projected_from |
  cites |
  supports |
  contradicts |
  supersedes |
  invalidates |
  proved_by |
  reviewed_by |
  gates |
  activates |
  generated |
  assigned_to
)

& [KernelRecord] is the common logical record envelope for every authority-kernel record
  + [record_id] is the durable surrogate identifier for one record instance
  + [record_kind] is one KernelRecordKind value
  + [natural_key] is the domain-meaning identity descriptor when meaningful, or a declared not_applicable or unresolved identity descriptor
  + [subject_ref] is the bounded subject the record is about
  + [authority_state] is one AuthorityState value
  + [source_ref_set] is the source, evidence, proof, or authority artifact references supporting the record
  + [lineage_edge_set] is the derivation, projection, citation, support, contradiction, supersession, invalidation, proof, review, gate, activation, generation, or assignment relation set
  + [freshness_rule] is the rule that classifies the record as current, stale, unknown, not_applicable, or invalidated
  + [status] is one RecordStatus value

  = must: include all nine common fields on every KernelRecord
  = must: reject a record envelope that omits record_id, record_kind, natural_key, subject_ref, authority_state, source_ref_set, lineage_edge_set, freshness_rule, or status
  = must: treat payload fields as record-kind-specific material owned by FSC1-S02 or later slices
  = must: keep common fields stable enough that physical storage can change without changing logical meaning

& [FieldContract: record_id] is the durable surrogate identity field
  + [field_name] is record_id
  + [field_requirement] is required
  + [field_value] is an immutable string unique inside the LangSOP authority-kernel namespace
  + [recommended_format] is krn:{record_kind}:{uuid}
  + [identity_role] is technical reference, not domain truth

  = must: remain stable for the lifetime of the record
  = must: be distinct from natural_key
  = must: survive physical storage migration unchanged
  - never: treat record_id as the only meaningful identity when a domain natural_key exists

& [FieldContract: record_kind] is the closed vocabulary field for record category
  + [field_name] is record_kind
  + [field_requirement] is required
  + [field_value] is one KernelRecordKind value
  + [schema_role] is selects the record-specific payload contract and lifecycle interpretation

  = must: be set before validating record-specific payload
  = must: be changed only by superseding the record, not by mutating the record in place
  - never: overload one record_kind to carry unrelated payload shapes

& [FieldContract: natural_key] is the domain identity descriptor
  + [field_name] is natural_key
  + [field_requirement] is required
  + [common_shape] is namespace, value, key_state, stability_window, identity_authority, and rationale
  + [key_state] is one NaturalKeyState value

  = must: preserve domain identity when it exists and remains meaningful
  = must: use key_state unresolved when identity is not yet known
  = must: use key_state not_applicable only with rationale
  = must: preserve prior natural_key through lineage when natural identity changes
  = must: defer record-specific natural-key rules to FSC1-S02
  - never: erase meaningful natural identity by relying only on record_id

& [FieldContract: subject_ref] is the bounded subject reference
  + [field_name] is subject_ref
  + [field_requirement] is required
  + [common_shape] is subject_namespace, subject_id, subject_label, and subject_scope
  + [scope_role] is identifies what the record is about without embedding the whole subject payload

  = must: point to a bounded subject, not a vague project area
  = must: preserve subject_scope when a record concerns a slice, chunk, capability, source, artifact, operator, surface, or proof
  = must: emit ambiguous_identity fault or blocked status when subject_ref cannot be resolved

& [FieldContract: authority_state] is the authority classification field
  + [field_name] is authority_state
  + [field_requirement] is required
  + [field_value] is one AuthorityState value
  + [default_for_nonclaim_records] is none

  = must: use none for purely mechanical or non-claim-bearing records
  = must: use source_only for preserved source that has not been interpreted into authority
  = must: use narrative_projection for narrative meaning that is derived but not governing implementation alone
  = must: use accepted_decision only when a decision has an explicit source_ref_set and scope
  = must: use signed_sjs only when a valid satisfaction signature with protocol UUID ad10f10f-d506-48ef-a805-f8b0a133766c is present
  = must: use proof_backed only when proof_result support is present or an explicit validated absence proof applies
  = must: use stale_projection when freshness_rule fails on derived material
  = must: use contradicted when support or proof conflicts with the record
  = must: use invalidated when the record no longer governs current work
  = must: use human_override only with explicit user source, scope, and override limit

& [FieldContract: source_ref_set] is the evidence and authority reference set
  + [field_name] is source_ref_set
  + [field_requirement] is required
  + [common_shape] is one or more SourceRef entries or an explicit empty_allowed rationale
  + [empty_allowed] is only for records whose authority_state is none and whose record_kind is mechanical trace material without claim-bearing content

  = must: be non-empty for source_only, narrative_projection, accepted_decision, signed_sjs, proof_backed, stale_projection, contradicted, invalidated, or human_override records
  = must: cite the preserved source for source-derived records
  = must: cite proof_result records for proof_backed records
  = must: cite invalidating or contradicting records when authority_state is contradicted or invalidated
  - never: accept trust-bearing records with silent or implied sources

& [SourceRef] is one source, proof, artifact, or authority reference
  + [source_ref_id] is a stable local reference identifier
  + [source_kind] is file, record, signature, proof, conversation_log, human_override, external_url, command_output, or explicit_absence
  + [source_locator] is path, record_id, URL, command name, or absence declaration
  + [source_hash] is required when the referenced file or generated artifact is intended to be immutable for validation
  + [source_scope] is the part of the source that supports the record

  = must: include enough locator material for later review
  = must: include hash when cited source stability matters to authority
  = must: preserve explicit_absence only when absence has been checked and recorded

& [FieldContract: lineage_edge_set] is the record relation set
  + [field_name] is lineage_edge_set
  + [field_requirement] is required
  + [common_shape] is zero or more LineageEdge entries
  + [empty_allowed] is only for root source records that cite preserved source in source_ref_set and have no derivation relation yet

  = must: be non-empty for derived projections, operator outputs, work packets, completion reviews, proof-backed records, stale projections, superseded records, contradicted records, and invalidated records
  = must: preserve derivation and projection edges separately
  = must: preserve contradiction, invalidation, and supersession edges as trace
  - never: collapse lineage into prose-only explanation when an edge can be declared

& [LineageEdge] is one typed relation from a record to another record, source, artifact, proof, or subject
  + [edge_kind] is one LineageEdgeKind value
  + [from_ref] is the record, source, artifact, proof, or subject where the relation begins
  + [to_ref] is the record, source, artifact, proof, or subject where the relation lands
  + [edge_scope] is the claim, field, payload, or state the relation concerns
  + [edge_rationale] is why the relation exists

  = must: preserve direction
  = must: cite source_ref_set when edge_rationale depends on external evidence
  = must: use invalidates, contradicts, or supersedes explicitly instead of replacing older records silently

& [FieldContract: freshness_rule] is the record currentness rule
  + [field_name] is freshness_rule
  + [field_requirement] is required
  + [common_shape] is freshness_state, freshness_subject_set, trigger_set, stale_action, and last_checked_ref
  + [freshness_state] is one FreshnessState value

  = must: define what makes the record stale or invalidated
  = must: use not_applicable only for immutable root records that cannot become stale under current authority rules
  = must: use unknown when no adequate freshness rule has been defined
  = must: mark derived projections stale when any source subject in freshness_subject_set changes
  = must: emit stale_projection or fault_record when stale_action cannot be safely applied

& [FieldContract: status] is the lifecycle status field
  + [field_name] is status
  + [field_requirement] is required
  + [field_value] is one RecordStatus value
  + [status_role] is operational lifecycle, distinct from authority_state and readiness_state

  = must: keep status distinct from authority_state
  = must: keep status distinct from readiness_state
  = must: preserve stale, superseded, contradicted, and invalidated states rather than deleting records
  = must: use blocked when required identity, authority, source, lineage, or freshness data is unresolved

& [KernelRecordInvariantSet] is the cross-record invariant set for KernelRecordCoreV1
  + [invariant] is all records include the nine common fields
  + [invariant] is record_id is immutable after creation
  + [invariant] is record_kind changes require supersession
  + [invariant] is natural_key does not replace record_id and record_id does not replace natural_key
  + [invariant] is claim-bearing and derived records require source_ref_set
  + [invariant] is derived, projected, proof-backed, stale, superseded, contradicted, and invalidated records require lineage_edge_set
  + [invariant] is freshness_rule must be explicit even when freshness_state is not_applicable
  + [invariant] is status, authority_state, and readiness_state are separate concepts
  + [invariant] is records are superseded or invalidated rather than rewritten when identity, authority, or proof changes materially

& [SchemaAcceptanceChecklist: KernelRecordCoreV1] is the FSC1-S01 verification checklist
  + [required_field_present] is record_id
  + [required_field_present] is record_kind
  + [required_field_present] is natural_key
  + [required_field_present] is subject_ref
  + [required_field_present] is authority_state
  + [required_field_present] is source_ref_set
  + [required_field_present] is lineage_edge_set
  + [required_field_present] is freshness_rule
  + [required_field_present] is status
  + [enum_present] is KernelRecordKind
  + [enum_present] is AuthorityState
  + [enum_present] is ReadinessState
  + [invariant_present] is lineage and freshness invariants
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is physical storage decision
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is runtime graph implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is surface implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is operations-control decision

  = must: accept FSC1-S01 only when all checklist items are satisfied
  = must: open FSC1-S02 only after this checklist is reviewed in a completion review

& [FSC1S01OutputBoundary] is the handoff boundary from FSC1-S01 to FSC1-S02
  + [accepted_output] is Kernel_Record_Core.v1.sop
  + [enables] is record-specific schema and natural-key matrix drafting
  + [does_not_enable] is storage backend decision without FSC1-S02 and FSC1-S03
  + [does_not_enable] is operator contract finalization without FSC1-S02
  + [does_not_enable] is runtime graph, surface, dispatch, or operations work

  = must: treat this file as a logical schema input, not runtime proof
